{"type":"standard","title":"Matt Little","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Matt Little</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q16731557","titles":{"canonical":"Matt_Little","normalized":"Matt Little","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Matt Little</span></span>"},"pageid":52620781,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/2026Little.jpg/330px-2026Little.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":443},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e6/2026Little.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":3004,"height":4032},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1377095645","tid":"bf84d529-babb-11f1-ac8a-9e35285ead3f","timestamp":"2026-09-27T21:38:16Z","description":"American attorney and politician (born 1984)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matt_Little","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matt_Little?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matt_Little?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Matt_Little"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matt_Little","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Matt_Little","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matt_Little?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Matt_Little"}},"extract":"Matthew Martin Little is an American attorney and politician and a former member of the Minnesota Senate. A member of the Minnesota Democratic–Farmer–Labor Party (DFL), he represented District 58 in the southern Twin Cities metropolitan area from 2017 to 2021. Little is the DFL nominee for the United States House of Representatives in Minnesota's 2nd congressional district in 2026. He received the party endorsement for the seat in May 2026 and won the DFL primary on August 11.","extract_html":"<p><b>Matthew Martin Little</b> is an American attorney and politician and a former member of the Minnesota Senate. A member of the Minnesota Democratic–Farmer–Labor Party (DFL), he represented District 58 in the southern Twin Cities metropolitan area from 2017 to 2021. Little is the DFL nominee for the United States House of Representatives in Minnesota's 2nd congressional district in 2026. He received the party endorsement for the seat in May 2026 and won the DFL primary on August 11.</p>"}